WEBVTT

00:01:02.190 --> 00:01:06.340
It's your fault for trying to race with 
Nagisa to see who could eat the watermelon faster.

00:01:06.660 --> 00:01:09.040
Then why just me?

00:01:13.660 --> 00:01:16.030
Nagisa has an iron stomach,

00:01:16.030 --> 00:01:18.220
so it was reckless of you 
to challenge her to a race.

00:01:49.910 --> 00:01:53.320
Good morning, Director.

00:01:54.450 --> 00:01:55.740
Good morning.

00:01:55.740 --> 00:01:57.560
About today's surgery...

00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:02.000
<i>Pretty Cure! Pretty Cure!</i>

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:04.800
<i>Pretty Cure Pretty Cure</i>

00:02:04.800 --> 00:02:07.640
<i>Pretty Cure Pretty Cure</i>

00:02:07.640 --> 00:02:11.910
<i>We're pretty and cure cure Together we are...</i>

00:02:11.910 --> 00:02:14.880
<i>PRETTY CURE...!</i>

00:02:14.880 --> 00:02:17.750
<i>Out of the frying pan, into the fire</i>

00:02:17.750 --> 00:02:19.650
<i>Frankly, it's totally unbelievable</i>

00:02:20.850 --> 00:02:23.550
<i>Even in our school in our 
school uniforms, we're both</i>

00:02:23.550 --> 00:02:25.160
<i>amazingly tough</i>

00:02:26.660 --> 00:02:30.960
<i>Each time we get out of a tight spot, we both</i>

00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:33.060
<i>become stronger</i>

00:02:33.060 --> 00:02:36.830
<i>and closer</i>

00:02:37.840 --> 00:02:40.840
<i>Yeah! Your best! My best! Because we're alive</i>

00:02:40.840 --> 00:02:43.410
<i>we never fail!</i>

00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:46.580
<i>Don't you know that good fortune 
comes to the gates of laughter?</i>

00:02:46.580 --> 00:02:49.450
<i>Out with the negative!</i>

00:02:49.450 --> 00:02:55.720
<i>Brighten up your life!
Try with all your might...</i>

00:02:55.720 --> 00:02:56.620
<i>Work like the devil!</i>

00:02:56.620 --> 00:02:59.320
<i>Pretty Cure! Pretty Cure!</i>

00:02:59.320 --> 00:03:02.130
<i>Pretty Cure! Pretty Cure!</i>

00:03:02.130 --> 00:03:05.030
<i>We're pretty and cure cure</i>

00:03:05.030 --> 00:03:06.600
<i>Together we are</i>

00:03:06.600 --> 00:03:09.670
<i>Pretty Cure...!</i>

00:03:14.920 --> 00:03:17.080
What floor is this new store on?

00:03:17.080 --> 00:03:18.470
Let me see... It's...

00:03:18.470 --> 00:03:19.300
It's on the 6th floor.

00:03:20.160 --> 00:03:23.280
Another assassin has 
appeared from Dotsuku Zone.

00:03:23.980 --> 00:03:26.840
Is that one of the seeds 
that Jyaku-King planted?

00:03:27.140 --> 00:03:29.030
So when Pollun said they were waking up,

00:03:29.030 --> 00:03:30.560
this is what he meant, isn't it?

00:03:31.690 --> 00:03:34.300
How many more will be waking up?

00:03:34.300 --> 00:03:35.790
How many altogether?

00:03:37.500 --> 00:03:39.880
In any case, we have to get out act together.

00:03:43.030 --> 00:03:45.610
I thought we were going to the 
sundries store on the top floor...

00:03:45.610 --> 00:03:46.340
Over there...

00:03:46.340 --> 00:03:47.660
Look... Look at that.

00:03:48.730 --> 00:03:51.360
Tomorrow is the Wakabadai Shrine Festival...

00:03:51.360 --> 00:03:54.080
The summer festival calls 
for a cotton kimono.

00:03:54.270 --> 00:03:55.790
That's true.

00:03:55.790 --> 00:04:00.210
I asked my mom to buy me a new 
cotton kimono this year, but...

00:04:00.210 --> 00:04:02.660
She said I can still wear 
the one from last year.

00:04:02.660 --> 00:04:05.880
Don't say that... It won't 
cost any money to look.

00:04:05.880 --> 00:04:06.790
Let's go!

00:04:07.170 --> 00:04:09.000
Isn't this cute?

00:04:10.640 --> 00:04:12.450
But isn't this one nice, too?

00:04:12.750 --> 00:04:14.160
I like that, too.

00:04:15.230 --> 00:04:16.560
This one is nice...

00:04:16.820 --> 00:04:18.570
How much is it?

00:04:20.270 --> 00:04:21.380
It's expensive.

00:04:21.830 --> 00:04:24.320
It's impossible, after all.

00:04:25.340 --> 00:04:28.540
I wonder what kind of "obi" sash would 
go with this year's cotton kimono.

00:04:28.980 --> 00:04:33.510
I really like the cotton kimono with the 
fireworks design that you sewed for me last year.

00:04:35.120 --> 00:04:38.620
But your dad and mom look forward to seeing

00:04:38.620 --> 00:04:43.970
what kind of cotton kimono 
you'll be wearing every year.

00:04:46.060 --> 00:04:52.230
And besides, I look forward to sewing 
your cotton kimono every year, too.

00:04:52.540 --> 00:04:53.940
Honoka?

00:04:54.250 --> 00:04:55.440
Nagisa?

00:04:55.440 --> 00:04:57.970
What a coincidence!

00:05:01.410 --> 00:05:05.980
"STORMY SUMMER FESTIVAL! 
THE THUNDER GOD IS SUPER SCARY?!"

00:05:08.720 --> 00:05:10.410
Okay... It's done.

00:05:10.700 --> 00:05:13.360
You know how to put on a kimono, too.

00:05:13.360 --> 00:05:15.380
My grandmother taught me how.

00:05:16.850 --> 00:05:18.880
I'll have to admit, I look cute in this.

00:05:19.240 --> 00:05:22.360
Are you sure it's okay for me to borrow 
such a beautiful cotton kimono?

00:05:22.360 --> 00:05:25.110
I only wore it once last year,

00:05:25.110 --> 00:05:28.650
so if you wear it, it'll 
make the kimono happy.

00:05:28.650 --> 00:05:29.680
Thank you.

00:05:30.090 --> 00:05:31.510
You're welcome.

00:05:31.510 --> 00:05:33.890
You're both beautiful, 
Nagisa and Honoka mipo.

00:05:33.890 --> 00:05:36.350
Not as cute as you, Mipple mepo.

00:05:36.350 --> 00:05:37.490
Mepple!

00:05:37.490 --> 00:05:38.910
Mipple!

00:05:41.060 --> 00:05:43.110
Shall we go then?

00:05:43.110 --> 00:05:44.080
I guess so.

00:05:44.970 --> 00:05:45.880
Where's Pollun?

00:05:49.970 --> 00:05:51.060
He's sleeping.

00:05:51.420 --> 00:05:54.090
He was so excited about the festival 
that he was running around earlier,

00:05:54.090 --> 00:05:56.440
yelling "It's a festival popo! 
It's a festival popo!" mipo.

00:05:56.440 --> 00:05:59.030
He got too carried away, 
and wore himself out mepo.

00:05:59.250 --> 00:06:01.220
Goro goro goro...

00:06:01.220 --> 00:06:02.230
Pikkan!

00:06:03.940 --> 00:06:05.450
He's talking in his sleep.

00:06:09.270 --> 00:06:11.320
Get up, Pollun mipo.

00:06:11.320 --> 00:06:13.080
Let's go to the festival together mepo.

00:06:13.750 --> 00:06:16.000
Popo... popo... popo...

00:06:16.780 --> 00:06:19.340
I feel bad about waking him up.

00:06:19.340 --> 00:06:22.750
It can't be helped. We'll 
have Pollun stay home.

00:06:24.170 --> 00:06:25.600
I'm home!

00:06:25.900 --> 00:06:27.230
Nagisa?

00:06:27.760 --> 00:06:30.710
You borrowed a really beautiful 
cotton kimono, didn't you?

00:06:31.980 --> 00:06:33.710
Thank you, Yukishiro-san.

00:06:33.710 --> 00:06:36.340
You're much better at putting 
on a kimono than I am.

00:06:36.680 --> 00:06:38.050
I'm not...

00:06:39.440 --> 00:06:40.320
Where's Ryota?

00:06:40.640 --> 00:06:44.920
His friend's father said he'd 
take him to the festival today,

00:06:44.920 --> 00:06:46.750
so he left a little while ago.

00:06:46.950 --> 00:06:50.150
All right! I can enjoy the festival 
this year without the little pest.

00:06:53.040 --> 00:06:54.720
We're leaving!

00:06:54.720 --> 00:06:56.030
Be careful!

00:06:56.030 --> 00:06:57.250
We will!

00:07:06.910 --> 00:07:08.280
Thanks for waiting.

00:07:16.480 --> 00:07:18.230
Nagisa!

00:07:19.950 --> 00:07:23.080
Mipple! Where are you popo?

00:07:43.690 --> 00:07:45.110
I recognize this smell...

00:07:45.400 --> 00:07:46.640
There you go.

00:07:47.860 --> 00:07:49.310
Akane-san!

00:07:49.310 --> 00:07:51.830
I've been waiting for you!

00:07:51.830 --> 00:07:53.350
Business is brisk, isn't it?

00:07:53.550 --> 00:07:55.760
Festivals are the busiest time of the year.

00:07:56.340 --> 00:07:58.310
But I'll give you all a discount.

00:07:58.600 --> 00:08:00.350
Really?

00:08:03.750 --> 00:08:05.380
We made out, didn't we?

00:08:07.540 --> 00:08:09.350
So you all came, too.

00:08:09.350 --> 00:08:10.500
Fujimura-kun!

00:08:12.100 --> 00:08:13.550
Just what you'd expect!

00:08:14.420 --> 00:08:15.860
You're kidding! It can't be!

00:08:15.860 --> 00:08:18.480
What happened to your usual great 
technique for scooping carp?

00:08:23.430 --> 00:08:26.490
Why do I get so nervous?

00:08:29.300 --> 00:08:32.190
Will you let these loose in the 
pond at your house, Honoka?

00:08:33.020 --> 00:08:33.880
Are you sure?

00:08:34.280 --> 00:08:36.360
Sis! Honoka-san!

00:08:36.570 --> 00:08:37.710
Ryota?

00:08:37.710 --> 00:08:40.340
You came just in time, Ryota-kun.

00:08:40.650 --> 00:08:42.500
What is it?

00:08:42.820 --> 00:08:44.730
Thank you!

00:08:45.170 --> 00:08:46.670
How lucky for you!

00:08:46.670 --> 00:08:49.000
A present from Honoka, the girl you adore!

00:08:51.110 --> 00:08:52.620
Ryota!

00:08:58.360 --> 00:08:59.680
He's such a brat.

00:09:04.830 --> 00:09:06.230
Goro goro...

00:09:06.230 --> 00:09:07.550
Pikkan!

00:09:07.550 --> 00:09:08.630
Dodo-n!!

00:09:09.370 --> 00:09:12.320
Hey! Have you heard about 
the rumor that a ghost

00:09:12.320 --> 00:09:14.030
comes out from the small shrine up there?

00:09:14.330 --> 00:09:16.260
I did... I heard it... I heard about it.

00:09:16.260 --> 00:09:19.260
If you go over there when it gets dark...

00:09:19.260 --> 00:09:21.440
You can hear the sound of someone crying...

00:09:29.710 --> 00:09:33.280
Come over here... Come over here...

00:09:35.380 --> 00:09:38.580
They scared themselves with their own story.

00:09:38.580 --> 00:09:39.980
Aren't you scared?

00:09:40.260 --> 00:09:41.290
Not at all...

00:09:41.290 --> 00:09:43.620
You're sure of yourself, aren't you?

00:09:43.620 --> 00:09:45.770
How about a test of courage?

00:09:47.500 --> 00:09:49.850
We'll pair up the boys and girls.

00:09:49.850 --> 00:09:51.340
Ready... set...

00:09:52.100 --> 00:09:54.570
Looks like we'll be together, Misumi-san.

00:09:56.920 --> 00:09:59.080
How did this happen?

00:09:59.800 --> 00:10:02.680
Let me explain the rules 
of the test of courage.

00:10:03.020 --> 00:10:06.300
We'll each go up the steps, 
and when you reach the top,

00:10:06.300 --> 00:10:09.890
you'll set the candles as an offering.

00:10:11.550 --> 00:10:13.090
When did you get that anyway?

00:10:13.400 --> 00:10:16.320
You had it all planned from 
the beginning, didn't you?

00:10:16.320 --> 00:10:19.490
But I didn't expect to have the girls along.

00:10:19.740 --> 00:10:21.800
You're kidding! It can't be!

00:10:22.850 --> 00:10:24.960
Are we going to be alone from here on?

00:10:25.170 --> 00:10:27.530
No way!

00:10:31.960 --> 00:10:33.270
Goro goro...

00:10:33.270 --> 00:10:34.220
Pikkan!

00:10:34.220 --> 00:10:35.610
Dodo-n!

00:10:42.360 --> 00:10:43.660
Goro goro...

00:10:43.660 --> 00:10:44.850
Pikkan!

00:10:44.850 --> 00:10:46.190
Dodo-n!

00:11:04.780 --> 00:11:06.830
I'm tired popo.

00:11:26.280 --> 00:11:29.820
In a situation like this, 
I should say something...

00:11:29.820 --> 00:11:31.540
But what?

00:11:31.910 --> 00:11:32.960
What's wrong?

00:11:32.960 --> 00:11:35.140
I thought you said you weren't 
afraid to take the test of courage.

00:11:35.400 --> 00:11:37.620
It's not what you think!

00:11:39.260 --> 00:11:41.540
The stone step is broken over there.

00:11:51.310 --> 00:11:52.390
Be careful.

00:11:52.670 --> 00:11:54.320
T-thanks.

00:12:02.890 --> 00:12:06.830
I used to play here a lot when 
I was little, but lately, I...

00:12:09.220 --> 00:12:11.380
I hear the cry of the green pine cricket.

00:12:11.830 --> 00:12:13.550
Summer is almost over, isn't it?

00:12:13.850 --> 00:12:15.780
I'm surprised you can tell the difference.

00:12:15.780 --> 00:12:18.830
What's the difference between a green 
pine cricket and a pine cricket?

00:12:19.150 --> 00:12:21.550
The cry of a pine cricket is "chinchirorin"

00:12:21.550 --> 00:12:25.360
whereas the green pine cricket 
sounds like, "ryuryu."

00:12:25.360 --> 00:12:26.350
For your information,

00:12:26.350 --> 00:12:29.820
the green pine cricket was first 
discovered in Japan in the Meiji era...

00:12:29.820 --> 00:12:31.890
It originally comes from China.

00:12:31.890 --> 00:12:34.590
You're in top form, aren't you?

00:12:34.590 --> 00:12:35.630
What do you mean?

00:12:35.630 --> 00:12:37.080
Nothing...

00:12:41.680 --> 00:12:43.010
We accomplished our mission.

00:12:44.720 --> 00:12:46.840
That was easy, wasn't it?

00:12:46.840 --> 00:12:48.780
Wait!

00:12:49.800 --> 00:12:51.820
Did you hear something?

00:12:53.240 --> 00:12:55.080
Nagisa!

00:12:55.080 --> 00:12:57.210
Fujimura-kun!

00:12:57.210 --> 00:12:59.820
It looks like it's going to rain!

00:13:01.240 --> 00:13:02.410
All right.

00:13:02.410 --> 00:13:03.890
Let's go back down.

00:13:07.070 --> 00:13:08.860
Wait popo!

00:13:15.850 --> 00:13:18.220
Let's go down before it starts raining.

00:13:26.290 --> 00:13:27.330
It's raining!

00:13:30.980 --> 00:13:32.000
Watch out!

00:13:41.160 --> 00:13:42.310
Fuji-P?

00:13:44.100 --> 00:13:45.420
This is terrible.

00:13:53.770 --> 00:13:56.050
We're almost there, Fuji-P...

00:13:56.050 --> 00:13:57.760
I'm sorry.

00:13:58.750 --> 00:14:00.440
What are you saying?

00:14:00.440 --> 00:14:02.680
If I hadn't slipped...

00:14:03.230 --> 00:14:05.750
To a soccer player, his legs are his life.

00:14:06.150 --> 00:14:08.720
It's because I didn't train properly...

00:14:08.890 --> 00:14:11.890
Nagisa! Fujimura-kun!

00:14:11.890 --> 00:14:13.420
Are you okay?

00:14:15.380 --> 00:14:19.470
Everybody! Fuji-P has been hurt.

00:14:20.540 --> 00:14:21.680
Nagisa?

00:14:27.380 --> 00:14:29.430
I can't get through.

00:14:29.430 --> 00:14:32.010
I was going to get someone to pick us up.

00:14:33.810 --> 00:14:35.690
Something sinister is coming mepo!

00:14:35.690 --> 00:14:37.730
It's getting closer and closer mipo!

00:14:44.430 --> 00:14:48.240
Please! Stop! Stop!

00:14:54.960 --> 00:14:56.250
What's wrong?

00:14:56.730 --> 00:14:57.920
Goro goro...

00:14:57.920 --> 00:14:59.160
Pikkan!

00:14:59.160 --> 00:15:00.200
Dodo-n!!

00:15:04.100 --> 00:15:05.090
Goro goro...

00:15:05.090 --> 00:15:06.180
Pikkan!

00:15:06.180 --> 00:15:07.660
Dodo-n!!

00:15:09.610 --> 00:15:12.190
Thank you so much.

00:15:12.190 --> 00:15:13.310
You're a life saver.

00:15:13.500 --> 00:15:18.080
I had business at the hospital, 
so it was just perfect.

00:15:19.610 --> 00:15:21.810
Are you okay, Fujimura-kun?

00:15:24.000 --> 00:15:25.260
I'm sorry.

00:15:25.560 --> 00:15:27.010
Forget about it already.

00:15:36.000 --> 00:15:38.110
Director... what's wrong?

00:15:38.630 --> 00:15:40.040
Director?

00:15:40.040 --> 00:15:43.690
Our orthopedic surgeon is an excellent 
doctor, so please don't worry.

00:15:48.970 --> 00:15:52.760
That man is the hospital 
director here, isn't he?

00:15:52.760 --> 00:15:54.620
We were lucky weren't we?

00:16:15.640 --> 00:16:18.450
I wonder if Fuji-P is okay.

00:16:18.450 --> 00:16:20.270
He's fine.

00:16:21.290 --> 00:16:23.820
I feel an awesome sinister 
presence here mepo.

00:16:23.820 --> 00:16:26.790
The presence is coming from the rooftop mipo.

00:16:41.350 --> 00:16:42.440
What's that?

00:16:42.440 --> 00:16:44.380
Don't tell me it's a new enemy!

00:16:49.690 --> 00:16:52.100
I won't tell you what's true.

00:16:52.760 --> 00:16:53.960
Who are you?

00:16:54.150 --> 00:16:58.650
Unfortunately, I have no time 
to deal with you two right now.

00:16:59.220 --> 00:17:01.670
Come to me, Zakenna!

00:17:14.380 --> 00:17:17.630
Zakenna!

00:17:18.450 --> 00:17:21.250
Nagisa! Honoka! Transform mipo!

00:17:27.410 --> 00:17:29.760
Dual Aurora Wave!

00:17:58.770 --> 00:18:01.050
Protector of the Light, Cure Black!

00:18:01.270 --> 00:18:03.650
Protector of the Light, Cure White!

00:18:05.740 --> 00:18:07.390
Together, we're Pretty Cure!

00:18:08.780 --> 00:18:10.790
Servants of the power of darkness...

00:18:11.800 --> 00:18:14.230
Go back to where you came from!

00:18:14.610 --> 00:18:16.670
Zakenna!

00:18:26.490 --> 00:18:28.190
Those are pretty good moves!

00:18:36.660 --> 00:18:38.700
Zakenna!

00:18:46.190 --> 00:18:47.100
White!

00:18:47.260 --> 00:18:48.180
Black!

00:18:48.920 --> 00:18:51.840
Zakenna!

00:18:54.580 --> 00:18:56.390
Zakenna!

00:18:57.750 --> 00:19:00.270
Za... kenna!

00:19:08.040 --> 00:19:11.130
Zakenna...

00:19:12.890 --> 00:19:14.760
Did he just destroy himself?

00:19:15.110 --> 00:19:16.030
Now mepo!

00:19:17.400 --> 00:19:19.000
Black Thunder!

00:19:19.520 --> 00:19:21.400
White Thunder!

00:19:28.100 --> 00:19:31.040
The beautiful souls of Pretty Cure...!

00:19:31.390 --> 00:19:34.010
...will crush the sinister hearts!

00:19:35.050 --> 00:19:38.310
Pretty Cure Marble Screw!

00:19:47.500 --> 00:19:50.980
Gomenna! Gomenna! Gomenna!

00:19:50.980 --> 00:19:53.120
Gomenna! Gomenna!

00:20:00.630 --> 00:20:02.030
Another one?

00:20:03.710 --> 00:20:05.090
With this, there are three of them.

00:20:18.530 --> 00:20:19.900
Director...?

00:20:23.250 --> 00:20:25.190
What's wrong, Head Nurse?

00:20:26.810 --> 00:20:29.630
The results of these tests...

00:20:29.860 --> 00:20:32.850
I'm so glad it was just a slight sprain.

00:20:33.080 --> 00:20:35.030
If I keep it immobilized 
for two or three weeks,

00:20:35.030 --> 00:20:36.890
it'll be good as new in no time.

00:20:36.890 --> 00:20:38.230
What a relief.

00:20:38.230 --> 00:20:40.290
I'm really sorry.

00:20:40.290 --> 00:20:41.550
I told you... don't worry about it.

00:20:43.060 --> 00:20:45.390
Here's our car.

00:20:53.730 --> 00:20:56.920
It turned out to be an 
awful festival, didn't it?

00:20:57.750 --> 00:21:00.220
Wait!

00:21:00.220 --> 00:21:01.370
It's a ghost!

00:21:03.160 --> 00:21:04.310
Popo...

00:21:04.310 --> 00:21:05.210
Pollun?

00:21:06.620 --> 00:21:07.580
Pollun!

00:21:07.580 --> 00:21:08.540
Pollun mipo!

00:21:08.540 --> 00:21:09.950
How did you get here?

00:21:09.950 --> 00:21:12.760
You went outside on your 
own again, didn't you?

00:21:13.020 --> 00:21:14.220
